; PP&S 2000/040 test disk.
; There is no SetPatch here on purpose: SetPatch loads 68040.library
; (MMULib), which turns the MMU on and marks the unused 32-bit addresses
; invalid, so ppiprobe could not look at them.
Echo "PP&S 2000/040 test disk"
ppiprobe
Echo ""
Echo "To try the memory module without burning a ROM, type: ppiload"
Echo "The machine reboots with the module installed; boot this disk again"
Echo "and check the memory list. Switching the power off removes it."
